/T (Plastic pollution has become one of the most pressing environmental issues, affecting not only land but also marine ecosystems. Every year, millions of tons of plastic waste end up in our oceans, devastating marine life. Animals often mistake plastic debris for food, which leads to starvation and fatal blockages in their digestive systems. Microplastics, tiny particles of broken-down plastic, have even entered the global food chain, posing potential health risks to humans.While plastic is incredibly durable and convenient, its improper disposal creates a long-lasting crisis. Addressing this challenge requires a collective effort, including reducing single-use plastics, improving global waste management systems, and shifting towards sustainable alternatives.)
