/Title (Q1. Direction:Read the passage carefully and answer the questions that follow. The modern world often celebrates speed as a virtue. Information travels instantly across continents,decisions are expected to be made rapidly, and efficiency is regarded as the hallmark of progress. Yet this relentless pursuit of speed has produced an unexpected paradox: while humanity possesses unprecedented access to information, it often lacks the patience required for reflection. The capacity for deep thought is increasingly threatened by a culture that rewards immediacy over contemplation.Historically, many transformative ideas)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 651 0 R
>>
endobj
702 0 obj
<<
/Title (emerged not from hurried action but from prolonged periods of intellectual incubation. Scientific breakthroughs, philosophical insights and artistic masterpieces frequently resulted from sustained engagement with complexity rather than quick conclusions. Reflection allows individuals to evaluate assumptions, identify biases and recognise nuances that may otherwise remain hidden. Moreover, the acceleration of communication has amplified the spread of misinformation. Information can now travel farther in seconds than truth can be verified in hours. In such an environment, critical thinking becomes not merely an academic skill but a civic responsibility. The challenge facing contemporary society is therefore not the scarcity of information but the cultivation of wisdom. Knowledge may be acquired rapidly, but wisdom requires time, discernment and intellectual humility.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 652 0 R
/Next 734 0 R
>>
endobj
703 0 obj
<<
/Title (Plastic pollution has become one of the most pressing environmental issues, affecting not only land but also marine ecosystems. Every year, millions of tons of plastic waste end up in our oceans, devastating marine life. Animals often mistake plastic debris for food, which leads to starvation and fatal blockages in their digestive systems. Microplastics, tiny particles of broken-down plastic, have even entered the global food chain, posing potential health risks to humans.While plastic is incredibly durable and convenient, its improper disposal creates a long-lasting crisis. Addressing this challenge requires a collective effort, including reducing single-use plastics, improving global waste management systems, and shifting towards sustainable alternatives.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 652 0 R
/Prev 734 0 R
>>
endobj
